a magic card known as Landstar Shot

246
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,557
Not only does this card
give my Brigadier a

247
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:03,840
fancy new musket It
boosts his power by 600.

248
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:08,357
All right, little buddy,
show him what you got.

249
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,040
Attack Siegfried directly.

250
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,320
Hold your fire, you little munchkin.

251
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,860
I have a truss.

252
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:19,780
It's called Wotan's Judgment, and
it stops your attack instantly.

253
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,457
That's because it lets me
switch any magic card I hold

254
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:26,800
in my hand with the top card
of my deck and resupple.

255
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:32,037
If that's what you consider your A-games,

256
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,826
then you're not going
to last too much longer.

257
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:41,560
Is it me, or is it getting hot in here?

258
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,980
Just make your move, wise guy.

259
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,000
Well, someone's all fired up.

260
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:49,180
Perhaps this will cool you off.

261
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,900
I slay Pot of Greed.

262
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:53,540
You know what that means, don't you?

263
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:57,860
I can draw two additional
cards from my deck.

264
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:02,320
Next, I play Erda's Guidance.

265
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:06,660
As the goddess of knowledge, she
controls the past, present and future.

266
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:11,900
The hand is the future, the field is the
present and the graveyard is the past.

267
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:20,157
Now, thanks to my Fraulein friend, I can
move one card from my hand to my graveyard.

268
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:24,760
And in exchange, I can transfer one
trap from the grave to the field.

269
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:28,940
That's weird.

270
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,554
He went through all of that
just to play some trap card?

271
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:35,140
That'll do for now. That's it?

272
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,397
He's not even going to summon a monster?

273
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:40,500
Whatever Siegfried's
strategy is, I don't get it.

274
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:41,560
What strategy?

275
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:46,102
That's the second time he
left himself wide open.

276
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:50,157
Perhaps Siegfried is just
waiting for the right card.

277
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,064
Like that magic card he
played in his last duel.

278
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:56,877
You mean the one he used to
beat Rex and Weevil in one turn?

279
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,820
Oh, no.

280
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,880
I know you're watching here, Kaiba.

281
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,002
So enjoy the show while you can.

282
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,820
Because soon it will be curtains for you.

283
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,610
Ahem.

284
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:18,060
I don't know if you noticed,
but the duel's over here.

285
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:23,677
You can at least have the courtesy to look
at me when I'm about to kick your butt,

286
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,590
wise guy!

287
00:17:24,673 --> 00:17:25,537
You'll have to forgive me.

288
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:27,561
I forgot you were standing there.

289
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:32,100
But with an opponent as dull and
forgettable as you, can you blame me? Huh?

290
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,555
What did you call me?

291
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:37,660
Dueling you is about as
interesting as watching grass grow.

292
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,520
Don't listen to him!

293
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:42,820
So this duel's too boring for you, huh?

294
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:46,748
Then I'll just have to make
things more interesting, won't I?

295
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,390
Now!

296
00:17:49,473 --> 00:17:54,300
I sacrificed my Brigadier of
Landstar so I can summon Jinzo!

297
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:05,480
And thanks to my Jinzo special ability,
all of your trap cards are useless!

298
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,817
Oh no!

299
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:14,560
Now Jinzo, attack this chunk directly!

300
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:23,120
Ask that for a little excitement.

301
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:26,364
Maybe now you'll show
Joey Wheeler some respect.

302
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:28,481
I'm not just another pretty face.

303
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:34,571
That's showing him, Joey.

304
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,740
You the man, dude.

305
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:38,477
I think I've embarrassed
you enough for now.

306
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,678
So go ahead, Ziggy.

307
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:43,760
You were much better off
when I was ignoring you.

308
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:45,500
But that's over.

309
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:48,074
Because now you've gotten my attention.

310
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:53,000
So not only will I defeat you,
but I'll send you down in flames.

311
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:56,100
Und it all begins now.

312
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,704
This card should look familiar.

313
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:03,820
It's the same one I used to
devastate the last two fools.

314
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:06,400
Oh no, not that! We were right.

315
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,940
Now I activate the magic card.

316
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,100
Ride of the Valkyries!

317
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:44,340
And I'm afraid your end
is only the beginning.
